WEBVTT

00:00:00.597 --> 00:00:01.470
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.855 --> 00:00:05.518
In this lesson, we cut a curtain fringe, parted in the middle,

00:00:05.468 --> 00:00:07.150
for a client with long hair,

00:00:07.419 --> 00:00:09.710
then trim the pieces that frame the face.

00:00:10.033 --> 00:00:12.590
You heard the reason for each step in the theory lesson.

00:00:12.833 --> 00:00:13.870
Here, we do it.

00:00:14.428 --> 00:00:15.241
Step one:

00:00:15.477 --> 00:00:16.281
preparation.

00:00:16.612 --> 00:00:17.721
Wash your hands.

00:00:17.822 --> 00:00:18.223
Combs,

00:00:18.173 --> 00:00:22.841
scissors and clips have been cleaned and disinfected after the previous client.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:26.841
Wrap a disposable neck strip, and only then fasten the cape.

00:00:27.469 --> 00:00:28.202
Step two:

00:00:28.502 --> 00:00:30.762
the consultation, while the hair is dry.

00:00:31.488 --> 00:00:33.854
Use your finger to lay the hair on the forehead,

00:00:33.804 --> 00:00:36.122
and show the client where the fringe will stop.

00:00:36.707 --> 00:00:40.532
For a curtain fringe, the shortest point usually touches the eyebrows,

00:00:40.482 --> 00:00:42.042
or sits a little below them.

00:00:42.711 --> 00:00:46.968
Ask the client whether she can blow-dry it every morning, whether she wears glasses,

00:00:46.918 --> 00:00:48.922
and whether she often ties her hair up.

00:00:49.172 --> 00:00:53.134
If she wears glasses, the fringe should stop a little above the frames,

00:00:53.084 --> 00:00:54.842
so the frames don't push it up.

00:00:55.236 --> 00:00:58.362
Lift the hair, and look for a cowlick at the front hairline.

00:00:58.690 --> 00:01:01.194
If there is one, tell the client beforehand,

00:01:01.144 --> 00:01:03.482
and leave the fringe longer on that side.

00:01:04.158 --> 00:01:04.858
Step three:

00:01:05.036 --> 00:01:06.218
the triangle section.

00:01:06.809 --> 00:01:09.338
The hair is lightly damp, and combed smooth.

00:01:09.675 --> 00:01:13.351
Place the tip of the tail comb at the corner of the forehead on this side,

00:01:13.301 --> 00:01:15.018
just above the end of the eyebrow,

00:01:15.265 --> 00:01:18.858
and draw a diagonal line up to the tip of the triangle on top of the head.

00:01:19.277 --> 00:01:21.098
Do exactly the same on the other side.

00:01:21.444 --> 00:01:24.698
Comb the hair inside the triangle straight down over the face.

00:01:24.987 --> 00:01:28.698
Comb the rest of the hair back and to the sides, and clip it neatly.

00:01:29.093 --> 00:01:30.058
Look from the front:

00:01:30.339 --> 00:01:32.378
the sides of the triangle must be equal.

00:01:32.887 --> 00:01:35.018
Then look at the amount of hair in the triangle.

00:01:35.546 --> 00:01:39.578
If the client wants a thick fringe, move the tip of the triangle back a little.

00:01:39.994 --> 00:01:44.778
If she wants a light, wispy fringe, take a shallower triangle, with less hair.

00:01:45.118 --> 00:01:46.378
Take less to begin with.

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:51.445
If it is not enough, you can add a thin layer from behind, but once it is cut,

00:01:51.395 --> 00:01:52.858
you can't give it back.

00:01:53.519 --> 00:01:54.395
Step four:

00:01:54.728 --> 00:01:56.715
the first cut, very long.

00:01:57.224 --> 00:02:00.555
Ask the client to close her eyes, and keep her head straight.

00:02:01.145 --> 00:02:04.955
Comb the fringe straight down the middle of the face, without tension.

00:02:05.538 --> 00:02:10.235
Your index and middle fingers lightly support the hair at the level of the tip of the nose.

00:02:10.401 --> 00:02:12.843
Cut straight across just below your fingers,

00:02:12.793 --> 00:02:17.355
with the blade parallel to your fingers, and the scissor tips pointing to the side,

00:02:17.384 --> 00:02:18.475
away from the eyes.

00:02:18.904 --> 00:02:20.875
This cut is only a temporary length.

00:02:21.058 --> 00:02:23.275
We will go shorter gradually, later.

00:02:23.562 --> 00:02:26.795
Because the hair is damp, it will shrink up once it is dry.

00:02:27.067 --> 00:02:31.275
So while it is wet, never cut to the exact length you agreed with the client.

00:02:31.928 --> 00:02:32.801
Step five:

00:02:32.978 --> 00:02:34.401
shaping the curtain fringe.

00:02:34.724 --> 00:02:36.881
Part the fringe in two, right in the middle.

00:02:37.137 --> 00:02:40.561
Take the half on this side, and comb it down beside the face.

00:02:40.903 --> 00:02:44.293
Place your fingers on a diagonal, from the middle of the forehead,

00:02:44.243 --> 00:02:45.761
sloping out to the cheekbone.

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:50.920
Cut along the outer edge of your fingers, with the blade parallel to your fingers,

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:51.441
low down,

00:02:51.523 --> 00:02:52.721
away from the eyes.

00:02:53.068 --> 00:02:56.549
Then do the other half, keeping exactly the same diagonal angle,

00:02:56.499 --> 00:02:58.801
and compare it with the side you just cut.

00:02:59.463 --> 00:03:00.340
Step six:

00:03:00.587 --> 00:03:02.020
the pieces around the face.

00:03:02.344 --> 00:03:03.620
Unclip the sides.

00:03:03.969 --> 00:03:08.260
Take a thin section in front of the ear, and comb it forward over the face.

00:03:08.847 --> 00:03:13.041
Place your fingers on a diagonal, continuing the diagonal of the fringe,

00:03:12.991 --> 00:03:14.020
down to the chin,

00:03:14.094 --> 00:03:15.780
or the collarbone, as agreed.

00:03:16.289 --> 00:03:20.660
Cut below your fingers, with the scissors pointing down, away from the face.

00:03:21.089 --> 00:03:23.220
Do the other side exactly the same way.

00:03:23.457 --> 00:03:27.940
Take only thin sections, so the long hair behind keeps all its thickness.

00:03:28.328 --> 00:03:31.248
Take too much, and when the client ties her hair up,

00:03:31.198 --> 00:03:34.340
a whole chunk of short hair will hang down on each side.

00:03:35.011 --> 00:03:35.872
Step seven:

00:03:36.194 --> 00:03:37.552
blow-dry the fringe.

00:03:38.232 --> 00:03:41.232
Dry the fringe first of all, because it dries fastest.

00:03:41.661 --> 00:03:43.952
Point the nozzle down along the hair shaft.

00:03:44.301 --> 00:03:46.592
Comb the fringe to the left, and dry;

00:03:46.948 --> 00:03:48.912
then comb it to the right, and dry.

00:03:49.421 --> 00:03:53.472
Do this a few times, so the roots lie down, even where there is a cowlick.

00:03:53.648 --> 00:03:56.745
Then use a small round brush, lift the roots gently,

00:03:56.695 --> 00:03:59.792
and curve the halves of the fringe out to the sides,

00:03:59.823 --> 00:04:00.912
away from the face.

00:04:01.566 --> 00:04:02.285
Step eight:

00:04:02.545 --> 00:04:03.565
refine it dry.

00:04:03.891 --> 00:04:06.285
Now you can see where the fringe really sits.

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:08.525
Ask the client to close her eyes.

00:04:08.784 --> 00:04:13.048
Go shorter gradually, a couple of millimeters at a time, then let go,

00:04:12.998 --> 00:04:13.965
and look again.

00:04:14.296 --> 00:04:16.045
Point cut to soften the ends:

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:18.672
scissor tips up, small snips into the ends,

00:04:18.622 --> 00:04:21.565
with your fingers between the scissors and the face.

00:04:21.822 --> 00:04:23.085
Don't point cut too deep.

00:04:23.721 --> 00:04:24.602
Step nine:

00:04:24.745 --> 00:04:25.722
check the balance.

00:04:26.029 --> 00:04:30.122
The client sits straight, head straight, eyes looking straight into the mirror.

00:04:30.546 --> 00:04:34.408
Hold both sides of the fringe, and compare them at the same landmark,

00:04:34.358 --> 00:04:35.402
at the cheekbones.

00:04:35.784 --> 00:04:38.282
Whichever side is longer, trim that side.

00:04:38.547 --> 00:04:41.002
Step back, and look at the whole face.

00:04:41.351 --> 00:04:42.442
Then ask the client:

00:04:42.870 --> 00:04:43.962
is this length okay?

00:04:44.609 --> 00:04:47.320
The three most common mistakes when cutting a fringe:

00:04:47.539 --> 00:04:48.520
watch out for them.

00:04:48.977 --> 00:04:49.480
One:

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:52.280
pulling the fringe down tight, then cutting.

00:04:52.609 --> 00:04:55.720
When you let go, it jumps up, shorter than you wanted.

00:04:56.212 --> 00:04:56.680
Two:

00:04:57.028 --> 00:05:00.760
cutting while the client is tilting her head, or looking down at her phone.

00:05:01.109 --> 00:05:03.560
When she sits up straight, the fringe is uneven.

00:05:04.055 --> 00:05:04.680
Three:

00:05:04.949 --> 00:05:07.320
taking hair too wide toward the temples.

00:05:07.623 --> 00:05:12.280
The fringe covers the whole face, looks heavy, and is very hard to fix.

00:05:12.842 --> 00:05:13.564
Step ten:

00:05:13.885 --> 00:05:14.684
the finish.

00:05:15.004 --> 00:05:18.357
Gently brush the loose hair off the face with a soft brush,

00:05:18.307 --> 00:05:20.204
before the client opens her eyes.

00:05:20.695 --> 00:05:23.244
Show the client how to blow-dry the fringe at home:

00:05:23.673 --> 00:05:28.178
dry the fringe first, while the hair is still wet, nozzle pointing down,

00:05:28.128 --> 00:05:29.724
comb it left, then right,

00:05:30.073 --> 00:05:33.404
then use a round brush to curve the halves out to the sides.

00:05:33.584 --> 00:05:37.484
Let the client hold the dryer, and try it once, right there in the chair.

00:05:37.993 --> 00:05:42.524
The longer a curtain fringe gets, the easier it is to live with, so tell the client:

00:05:42.824 --> 00:05:45.209
if she wants to grow it out, just let it grow,

00:05:45.159 --> 00:05:47.644
and it will blend into the hair around the face.

00:05:48.156 --> 00:05:49.564
Write it in the client record:

00:05:49.853 --> 00:05:52.924
how long the fringe is, and which side has a cowlick.

00:05:53.353 --> 00:05:55.484
And book a fringe trim after a few weeks.

00:05:55.665 --> 00:06:00.656
After the client leaves, combs, scissors and clips are cleaned and disinfected,

00:06:00.606 --> 00:06:02.844
as in the lesson on cleaning tools.

00:06:03.193 --> 00:06:06.204
And now, please take the short quiz below the video.
